      _push(`<section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-teal to-teal/80 text-white py-20 px-4" data-v-3df17458><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center" data-v-3df17458><h1 class="text-5xl font-bold mb-6" data-v-3df17458>GDPR Compliance</h1><p class="text-xl opacity-90" data-v-3df17458> General Data Protection Regulation compliance for EU users </p><p class="text-sm opacity-75 mt-4" data-v-3df17458> Last updated: November 18, 2025 </p></div></section><section class="py-20 px-4 bg-white" data-v-3df17458><div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto prose prose-lg" data-v-3df17458><h2 data-v-3df17458>1. Introduction</h2><p data-v-3df17458> The General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is a comprehensive data protection law that applies to the processing of personal data of individuals in the European Union. At Classsemble, we are committed to full compliance with GDPR requirements and protecting the privacy rights of our EU users. </p><p data-v-3df17458> This document outlines our GDPR compliance measures and explains your rights under the regulation when using our educational collaboration platform. </p><h2 data-v-3df17458>2. Legal Basis for Processing</h2><p data-v-3df17458> Under GDPR, we must have a lawful basis for processing your personal data. We rely on the following legal bases: </p><h3 data-v-3df17458>2.1 Contract Performance (Article 6(1)(b))</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Providing our Canvas LMS integration services</li><li data-v-3df17458>Enabling course collaboration features</li><li data-v-3df17458>Facilitating meeting scheduling and communication</li><li data-v-3df17458>Processing payments for institutional subscriptions</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>2.2 Legitimate Interests (Article 6(1)(f))</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Service improvement and optimization</li><li data-v-3df17458>Security monitoring and fraud prevention</li><li data-v-3df17458>Customer support and technical assistance</li><li data-v-3df17458>Business analytics (using anonymized data)</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>2.3 Legal Obligation (Article 6(1)(c))</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Compliance with educational privacy laws (FERPA)</li><li data-v-3df17458>Data retention for audit purposes</li><li data-v-3df17458>Response to legal requests</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>2.4 Consent (Article 6(1)(a))</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Optional analytics and improvement features</li><li data-v-3df17458>Marketing communications (where permitted)</li><li data-v-3df17458>Third-party integrations beyond core functionality</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>3. Your GDPR Rights</h2><p data-v-3df17458> As an EU data subject, you have the following rights under GDPR: </p><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.1 Right of Access (Article 15)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Request confirmation of whether we process your personal data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Obtain a copy of your personal data we hold</li><li data-v-3df17458>Receive information about how we process your data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Learn about data retention periods and your other rights</li></ul><p data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>How to exercise:</strong> Email <a href="mailto:gdpr@classsemble.com" data-v-3df17458>gdpr@classsemble.com</a> with your access request</p><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.2 Right to Rectification (Article 16)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Correct inaccurate personal data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Complete incomplete personal data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Update your profile information</li></ul><p data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>How to exercise:</strong> Update your profile in the platform or contact support</p><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.3 Right to Erasure (Article 17)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Request deletion of your personal data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Have data removed when no longer necessary</li><li data-v-3df17458>Withdraw consent for consent-based processing</li></ul><p data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>How to exercise:</strong> Contact your educational institution or email <a href="mailto:gdpr@classsemble.com" data-v-3df17458>gdpr@classsemble.com</a></p><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.4 Right to Restrict Processing (Article 18)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Limit how we process your data while verifying accuracy</li><li data-v-3df17458>Restrict processing when you object to our legitimate interests</li><li data-v-3df17458>Maintain data instead of deletion for legal claims</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.5 Right to Data Portability (Article 20)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Receive your data in a structured, machine-readable format</li><li data-v-3df17458>Transfer your data to another service provider</li><li data-v-3df17458>Request direct transmission where technically feasible</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.6 Right to Object (Article 21)</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Object to processing based on legitimate interests</li><li data-v-3df17458>Object to direct marketing (if applicable)</li><li data-v-3df17458>Object to automated decision-making and profiling</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>3.7 Rights Related to Automated Decision Making (Article 22)</h3><p data-v-3df17458> We do not engage in automated decision-making or profiling that produces legal effects or significantly affects you. Any automated processing is limited to technical functionality and service optimization. </p><h2 data-v-3df17458>4. Data Protection Measures</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>4.1 Technical Safeguards</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Encryption:</strong> All data encrypted in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256)</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Access Controls:</strong> Role-based access with multi-factor authentication</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Monitoring:</strong> Continuous security monitoring and intrusion detection</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Backup Security:</strong> Encrypted backups with secure key management</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>4.2 Organizational Measures</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Staff Training:</strong> Regular GDPR and privacy training for all personnel</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Data Processing Agreements:</strong> Contracts with all data processors</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Privacy by Design:</strong> Privacy considerations in all system development</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Regular Audits:</strong> Internal and external privacy compliance audits</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>4.3 Data Minimization</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Collect only data necessary for service provision</li><li data-v-3df17458>Regularly review and purge unnecessary data</li><li data-v-3df17458>Implement privacy-preserving analytics</li><li data-v-3df17458>Limit data access to authorized personnel only</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>5. International Data Transfers</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>5.1 Transfer Safeguards</h3><p data-v-3df17458> When transferring EU personal data to countries outside the EEA, we implement appropriate safeguards: </p><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Standard Contractual Clauses:</strong> EU Commission-approved SCCs with data processors</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Adequacy Decisions:</strong> Transfers only to countries with adequacy decisions where applicable</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Additional Safeguards:</strong> Technical measures beyond contractual protections</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>5.2 US Data Processing</h3><p data-v-3df17458> Our primary data processing occurs in the United States. We ensure adequate protection through: </p><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Standard Contractual Clauses with supplementary measures</li><li data-v-3df17458>Regular assessments of US surveillance law impacts</li><li data-v-3df17458>Technical measures including encryption and pseudonymization</li><li data-v-3df17458>Contractual guarantees from service providers</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>6. Data Retention</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>6.1 Retention Periods</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Active Student Data:</strong> Duration of course enrollment plus 1 academic year</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Completed Course Data:</strong> 3 years after course completion</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Account Data:</strong> Until account deletion or 7 years of inactivity</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Communication Data:</strong> 2 years or until deletion request</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Analytics Data:</strong> Anonymized after 6 months, retained for 2 years</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>6.2 Deletion Process</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Automated deletion based on retention schedules</li><li data-v-3df17458>Secure deletion methods that render data unrecoverable</li><li data-v-3df17458>Documentation of deletion activities</li><li data-v-3df17458>Verification of complete data removal</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>7. Data Breach Procedures</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>7.1 Breach Response</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Detection:</strong> Automated monitoring and staff reporting procedures</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Assessment:</strong> Risk evaluation within 24 hours of discovery</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Containment:</strong> Immediate steps to limit breach scope</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Investigation:</strong> Forensic analysis to determine cause and extent</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>7.2 Notification Requirements</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Supervisory Authority:</strong> Notification within 72 hours if required</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Data Subjects:</strong> Notification without undue delay if high risk</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Institutional Partners:</strong> Immediate notification to affected schools</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Documentation:</strong> Comprehensive breach records maintained</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>8. Privacy by Design and Default</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>8.1 Design Principles</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Proactive:</strong> Privacy protection built into system design</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Privacy as Default:</strong> Highest privacy settings by default</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Full Functionality:</strong> Privacy without compromising educational features</li><li data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>End-to-End Security:</strong> Protection throughout data lifecycle</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>8.2 Implementation</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Privacy impact assessments for new features</li><li data-v-3df17458>Minimal data collection by default</li><li data-v-3df17458>User-friendly privacy controls</li><li data-v-3df17458>Regular privacy compliance reviews</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>9. Children&#39;s Data Protection</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>9.1 Age Verification</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Reliance on educational institution age verification</li><li data-v-3df17458>Special protections for users under 16</li><li data-v-3df17458>Parental consent procedures where required</li><li data-v-3df17458>Enhanced privacy protections for minors</li></ul><h3 data-v-3df17458>9.2 Special Safeguards</h3><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Reduced data collection for minor users</li><li data-v-3df17458>No behavioral advertising or profiling</li><li data-v-3df17458>Enhanced deletion rights</li><li data-v-3df17458>Regular review of child data processing</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>10. Supervisory Authority</h2><h3 data-v-3df17458>10.1 Lead Supervisory Authority</h3><p data-v-3df17458> For GDPR purposes, our lead supervisory authority is determined by our main establishment in the EU or our EU representative. </p><h3 data-v-3df17458>10.2 Right to Lodge Complaints</h3><p data-v-3df17458> You have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, particularly in the EU member state where you: </p><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Have your habitual residence</li><li data-v-3df17458>Have your place of work</li><li data-v-3df17458>Believe an infringement of GDPR has occurred</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>11. Data Protection Officer</h2><div class="bg-teal/10 border-l-4 border-teal p-6 rounded-r-lg" data-v-3df17458><p data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>EU Data Protection Officer</strong></p><p data-v-3df17458>Email: <a href="mailto:dpo@classsemble.com" class="text-teal hover:underline" data-v-3df17458>dpo@classsemble.com</a></p><p data-v-3df17458>The DPO is responsible for:</p><ul class="mt-2" data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Monitoring GDPR compliance</li><li data-v-3df17458>Conducting privacy impact assessments</li><li data-v-3df17458>Serving as contact point for supervisory authorities</li><li data-v-3df17458>Providing guidance on privacy matters</li></ul></div><h2 data-v-3df17458>12. Regular Compliance Review</h2><ul data-v-3df17458><li data-v-3df17458>Annual GDPR compliance audits</li><li data-v-3df17458>Regular updates to policies and procedures</li><li data-v-3df17458>Staff training on GDPR requirements</li><li data-v-3df17458>Technology updates to enhance privacy protection</li></ul><h2 data-v-3df17458>13. Contact for GDPR Matters</h2><p data-v-3df17458> For any GDPR-related questions or to exercise your rights, contact us: </p><div class="bg-teal/20 border-l-4 border-teal p-6 rounded-r-lg mt-6" data-v-3df17458><p data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>GDPR Compliance Team</strong></p><p data-v-3df17458>Email: <a href="mailto:gdpr@classsemble.com" class="text-teal hover:underline" data-v-3df17458>gdpr@classsemble.com</a></p><p data-v-3df17458>Address: 123 Education Street, San Francisco, CA 94102</p><p data-v-3df17458>EU Representative: [To be appointed if/when required]</p></div><p class="mt-8 p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg" data-v-3df17458><strong data-v-3df17458>Response Time:</strong> We will respond to your GDPR requests within 30 days. In complex cases, we may extend this by an additional 60 days with explanation. </p></div></section>`);
